# Tracey Bootstrap Compiler Documentation

This directory contains the documentation for the Tracey bootstrap compiler (`traceyc`)
and its experimental internal toolchain (assembler + linker).

## Contents

- `architecture.md` — overall compiler architecture and pipeline.
- `build.md` — build instructions, configuration, silent build.
- `lexer.md` — lexical analysis specification.
- `parser.md` — parser and AST specification.
- `semantic.md` — semantic analysis and type checking.
- `codegen.md` — code generation (AArch64).
- `assembler.md` — internal AArch64 assembler.
- `linker.md` — internal ELF64 AArch64 linker.
- `usage.md` — end-to-end usage examples.
- `testing.md` — running and adding tests.
- `maintenance.md` — coding style, formatting, and maintenance.

## Project status

Tracey is in the bootstrap stage. The compiler currently supports a minimal
subset of the language: functions, local variables, `if`/`while`, arithmetic,
comparisons, logical operators, and `return`. The internal assembler/linker
support AArch64 Linux only. The compiler automatically invokes the assembler
and linker and produces `a.out` by default.
